+# Local Base Fork
+
+The old onboarding note is wrong about both the command and the sanity check.
+
+## What goes wrong
+
+`yarn fork base` does not fork Base in this checkout. It falls through to the
+Foundry workspace fork script without passing `base` as the script's `$1`, so
+the workspace default is used instead:
+
+```json
+// package.json
+"fork": "yarn foundry:fork",
+"foundry:fork": "yarn workspace @se-2/foundry fork"
+```
+
+```json
+// packages/foundry/package.json
+"fork": "make fork FORK_URL=${1:-mainnet}"
+```
+
+I verified this by running the command with a temporary `HOME`; it printed:
+
+```text
+anvil --fork-url mainnet --chain-id 31337
+```
+
+That `mainnet` value is the Ethereum mainnet RPC alias, not Base:
+
+```toml
+# packages/foundry/foundry.toml
+mainnet = "https://eth-mainnet.alchemyapi.io/v2/${ALCHEMY_API_KEY}"
+base = "https://mainnet.base.org"
+```
+
+So the node can be alive and mining while still mirroring the wrong chain.
+The Base USDC address, `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`, is a
+contract on Base. On an Ethereum mainnet fork that address has no token
+contract, so reads against it come back empty.
+
+## Correct command
+
+From the repo root, run the Makefile target through the Foundry workspace and
+set `FORK_URL`:
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @se-2/foundry exec make fork FORK_URL=base
+```
+
+The Makefile target uses that value as Anvil's fork source:
+
+```make
+# packages/foundry/Makefile
+fork: setup-anvil-wallet
+	anvil --fork-url ${FORK_URL} --chain-id 31337
+```
+
+`base` resolves through `packages/foundry/foundry.toml` to:
+
+```toml
+base = "https://mainnet.base.org"
+```
+
+If you want to avoid relying on the alias, this is equivalent:
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @se-2/foundry exec make fork FORK_URL=https://mainnet.base.org
+```
+
+## Useful sanity check
+
+Do not use `cast chain-id` for this. The Makefile always starts Anvil with
+`--chain-id 31337`, so a Base fork, an Ethereum mainnet fork, and a non-forked
+local chain can all answer with the same local chain id.
+
+Check for the Base USDC contract instead:
+
+```bash
+cast call --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
+  0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 \
+  'symbol()(string)'
+```
+
+Expected output on a Base fork:
+
+```text
+"USDC"
+```
+
+For one more assertion:
+
+```bash
+cast call --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
+  0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 \
+  'decimals()(uint8)'
+```
+
+Expected output:
+
+```text
+6
+```
+
+Those calls distinguish the chain state we actually need: the local node is
+forking a chain where Base USDC is deployed at the expected address.

